body:
When adding a transformData function to a refinement list, it is not factored in when sorting the refinements. The bug is reproduced here: https://jsfiddle.net/9ej3v2t6/

1. added a refinement list widget for genres.
2. added transformData function that changes the label of one of the genres from "Comedy" to "Humor"
3. added `sortBy:['name:asc']` and would expect the refinements to be sorted correctly but we get Action, **Humor**, Crime etc.

This problem can be circumvented by using a custom function for sortBy, something like this:


```
sortBy: function(a,b){
  const genres = {'Comedy':'Humor'};
  var nameA = a.name.toUpperCase(); // ignore upper and lowercase
  var nameB = b.name.toUpperCase(); // ignore upper and lowercase

  if (genres.hasOwnProperty(a.name)) nameA = genres[a.name].toUpperCase();
  if (genres.hasOwnProperty(b.name)) nameB = genres[b.name].toUpperCase();

  if (nameA < nameB) {
    return -1;
  }
  if (nameA > nameB) {
    return 1;
  }
 // names must be equal
 return 0;
}
```
